00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now I thought I'd share
some of my favorite

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:04.604
Turkey Day tradition stories
from you guys. Here we go.

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:07.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
This first one
is from @luckylizzy.

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:09.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
She says, "My mom makes us
get up at 4:00 a.m.

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:10.877 line:92%
to dance with the raw Turkey,

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:12.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
holding it
by its wings and legs,

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:16.049
because it tenderizes the turkey
before it goes in the oven.

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:19.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
33 years now,
just dancing with the turkey."

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:21.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
There you go, yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:22.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Lucky.
-It's a tradition.

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:24.357 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-She's lucky.

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:26.259 line:92%
-This one's from @thesophiashow.

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:29.095
She says, "My dad, brother,
and grandpa always fight

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:29.763 size:78% position:39% line:92%
over the turkey neck.

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:32.665
To settle it, my grandma throws
it over her head backwards

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:35.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
and has them try to catch it
like a bridal bouquet."

00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:39.672 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:42.042 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-They're neck and neck.

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:44.144 line:92%
-This one's from @megimonster.

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:47.380 align:start size:94% position:6%
She says, "My family has
a tradition called 'ham slap,'

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:48.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you take
a piece of ham

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:51.785
and slap an unsuspecting family
member in the face with it

00:00:51.785 --> 00:00:54.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
while yelling,
'You just got ham slapped!'"

00:00:54.587 --> 00:01:01.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Yeah!

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:06.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You just got ham slapped.
-Pcht!

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:08.601 line:92%
-This one's from @myjowilson.

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:11.071
She says, "Every time
someone gets nostalgic and says,

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:12.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Do you remember,'
my twin brother and I

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:14.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
meet in the kitchen
and secretly do a shot.

00:01:14.374 --> 00:01:17.243
It's makes hearing the same
old stories way more fun."

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:20.113 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:21.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would start saying,
"Do you remember"

00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:23.316
just to get them wasted.
-Keep on remembering stuff.

